<title>UK: Britain captures 25 pct of world defence market.</title>
<headline>Britain captures 25 pct of world defence market.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain captured a record share of the world defence market last year and now accounts for 25 percent of sales, Defence Procurement Minister James Arbuthnot said on Friday.</p>
<p>Britain is now second only to the United States which captured 34 percent of world trade in guns, fighter planes, helicopters and other defence equipment.</p>
<p>&quot;1996 was another very successful year for British defence companies with a provisional figure of 5.1 billion pounds ($8.26 billion) worth of business achieved during the year,&quot; Arbuthnot said in a statement. &quot;This represents 25 percent of the world market, an all-time record for the UK and compares with figures of 16 percent in 1994 and 19 percent in 1995,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
